5. Hero section — reflective image slideshow
This is the defining feature of the GVCC website.






















11














The entire first screen should feature a full-width image slideshow using the actual photographs from CHURCH.pdf.
Image source
Use the actual photographs from the supplied PDF. Do not replace the church's real photographs with stock church photographs.

All available photos should be extracted, organized, optimized and used in the website.
Slideshow behavior
- Full viewport height on desktop.
- Approximately 85–100vh.
- Responsive height on mobile.
- Automatic transition every 6–9 seconds.
- Crossfade between images.
- Slow zoom effect.
- Dark gradient overlay.
- Optional subtle blur on background transitions.
- Manual previous/next controls.
- Pause/resume slideshow.
- Slide indicator.
- Support swipe gestures on mobile.
- Respect prefers-reduced-motion.
Image transition effects
Use a combination of:
- Fade in/out.
- Slow zoom in.
- Slight horizontal movement.
- Ken Burns effect.
- Soft cinematic transitions.
Do not use aggressive transitions, flashing effects or rapid movement.
Slideshow image handling
The pictures should not all be displayed with the same crop.

Use:
- object-fit: cover for immersive backgrounds.
- Responsive focal positioning.
- object-position to preserve the important subject.
- Portrait images positioned carefully.
- Desktop and mobile-specific crop behavior where necessary.
A preacher should not be cropped out of a photo. The main subjects must remain visible.

